Attribution chain
-----------------

This work builds on two prior published models. Both must be credited when
this design is redistributed or adapted.

1. "Stevenson Screen" by Thingiverse user raingel
   https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:3486326
   Licence: CC BY 4.0

2. "Stevenson Shield (mini)" by Thingiverse user commonslabgr
   https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:4915068
   Licence: Creative Commons - Attribution (per LICENSE.txt supplied in the
   downloaded package, reproduced verbatim in upstream/LICENSE.txt)
   A remix of (1), reduced in size and reworked for field robustness and
   sensor serviceability.

3. This work — SHT4x Stevenson radiation shield (FieldMesh)
   Modified from (2). Changes are listed below.
   Licence: CC BY 4.0


Changes made in this work
-------------------------

Starting from the `stevenson_cap.stl` mesh of (2), applied by script
(`modify_thingiverse_stevenson_sht40.py`, run under Blender):

- Added a top collar to the original cap to receive a separate PG7 clamp
  flange.
- Bored the collar to clear the SHT4x probe body and the already-tightened
  under-flange gland nut envelope.
- Added a printed PG7 retainer flange as a new separate part
  (`sht40_pg7_retainer_flange.stl`) — a plain clamp plate, not a hex nut trap.
- Added a right-angle bracket adapter as a new separate part
  (`sht40_right_angle_bracket_adapter.stl`) for horizontal mounting.
- Added unified mount feet matching the FieldMesh shared sensor deck
  (64 mm two-hole M3 interface).

The original `stevenson_base.stl` of (2) is not used in the normal two-piece
build; it is retained in `upstream/` for reference only.


Provenance of the upstream files
--------------------------------

The unmodified source meshes and the licence and readme text supplied by the
upstream author are reproduced in `upstream/`, so this design can be
regenerated from source without a manual download. Redistribution of those
files is permitted by CC BY, subject to the attribution above.
